    "shortSuggestedAnswer": "| Scenario | Purpose of Funds Received | Banking Treatment | Statutory Outcome (Clause 10 Part I Second Schedule) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **(a) M/s Ram & Co. (\u20b910 Lakhs)** | Trust money for investment in specified securities | Deposited in firm's own savings bank account for 3 months | **GUILTY of Professional Misconduct** (Failed to open separate client account) |\n| **(b) CA N (\u20b92.00 Lakhs)** | Advance to meet estimated out-of-pocket branch tour expenses | Deposited into personal account and utilized for travel | **NOT GUILTY** (Expressly exempted as money meant to be expended) |\n\n```\n[Clause (10) Client Funds Classification]\n                Moneys Received from Client\n                             \u2502\n       \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n       \u25bc                                           \u25bc\nClient Money for Specific Purposes          Advance Fees / Expense Reimbursement\n(Investments, Tax Payments, Escrow)         (Out-of-pocket tour advance, retainers)\n       \u2502                                           \u2502\n       \u25bc                                           \u25bc\nMANDATORY: Separate Bank Account            EXEMPTED from Clause (10)\n(No Commingling with Personal Funds)        (Can be deposited in normal accounts)\n```\n\n\u2022 **Statutory Principles under Clause (10) of Part I of Second Schedule**:\n  1. **Legal Mandate**: A CA is guilty of misconduct if he fails to keep moneys of his clients (other than fees/remuneration or money meant to be expended) in a separate banking account, or fails to use such moneys for the intended purpose within a reasonable time.\n  2. **Analysis**:\n     - *Case (a)*: \u20b910 lakhs was client investment money. Depositing it in the firm's savings account commingles client funds with firm funds. M/s Ram & Co. is **GUILTY**.\n     - *Case (b)*: \u20b92 lakhs was an advance against estimated travel expenses (\"money meant to be expended\"). Clause (10) expressly excludes such advances. CA N is **NOT GUILTY**.",
