    "shortSuggestedAnswer": "| Parameter | Calculation / Statutory Rule | Evaluation for M/s XYZ & Co. |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Number of Partners** | 6 Partners | Firm has 6 active partners |\n| **Individual Quota per Partner** | 60 tax audits / partner | Prescribed under Chapter VI of Guidelines |\n| **Firm Aggregate Ceiling** | 6 \u00d7 60 = **360 Tax Audits** | Maximum permissible tax audits for the firm |\n| **Audits Signed by Mr. Gaurav** | 290 tax audits | Signed on behalf of the firm |\n| **Audits Signed by Other 5 Partners**| 5 \u00d7 14 = 70 tax audits | Signed on behalf of the firm |\n| **Total Audits Signed by Firm** | 290 + 70 = **360 Tax Audits** | Exactly equals the firm ceiling (**<= 360**) |\n| **Misconduct Verdict** | **NOT GUILTY of Professional Misconduct** | Aggregate limit has not been breached |\n\n```\n[Tax Audit Ceiling Aggregation Mechanism (Section 44AB)]\n                  M/s XYZ & Co. (6 Partners)\n                              \u2502\n                              \u25bc\n           Firm Quota = 6 Partners \u00d7 60 = 360 Audits\n                              \u2502\n       \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n       \u25bc                                             \u25bc\nSigned by Mr. Gaurav: 290                     Signed by 5 Partners: 70\n       \u2502                                             \u2502\n       \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                              \u25bc\n                  Total Signed = 360 Audits\n             (Does NOT exceed 360 firm ceiling)\n                              \u25bc\n             NOT GUILTY of Professional Misconduct\n```\n\n\u2022 **Statutory Principles under Council General Guidelines, 2008**:\n  1. **Ceiling Limit**: A member in practice shall not accept more than 60 tax audit assignments under Section 44AB per financial year.\n  2. **Firm Distribution Flexibility**: In the case of a firm of CAs, the specified number of tax audit assignments is **60 per partner in aggregate**. The Council clarification allows partners to sign reports in any mutually agreed distribution, provided the overall firm ceiling (360) is not exceeded.\n  3. **Conclusion**: Since the total reports signed (290 + 70 = 360) did not exceed 360, **Mr. Gaurav is NOT GUILTY of professional misconduct**.",
