    "shortSuggestedAnswer": "| Operational Parameter | Regulatory Requirement under ICAI UDIN Guidelines |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Statutory Authority** | Mandated by Council of ICAI under Section 15 of CA Act, 1949 |\n| **Applicability Scope** | All Certificates, GST & Tax Audit Reports, and Financial Audit Reports |\n| **Generation Deadline** | At the time of signing, or **within 60 DAYS** from the date of signing |\n| **Revocation Mechanism** | Permissible by clicking 'Revoke' and submitting **mandatory written reasons** |\n| **Non-Compliance Penalty** | **GUILTY of Professional Misconduct** under Clause (1) Part II of Second Schedule |\n\n```\n[UDIN Workflow & Lifecycle]\nDraft Report / Certificate Signed by Practicing CA\n                         \u2502\n                         \u25bc\n        Generate 18-Digit UDIN on UDIN Portal\n    (At time of signing or within MAXIMUM 60 DAYS)\n                         \u2502\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u25bc                                 \u25bc\nMention UDIN on Document          Failure to Generate UDIN\nShared with Client / Regulators   Within 60 Days\n        \u2502                                 \u2502\n        \u25bc                                 \u25bc\n   FULL VALIDITY                  PROFESSIONAL MISCONDUCT\n(Verifiable by Banks/MCA)         (Clause 1 Part II Second Schedule)\n```\n\n\u2022 **Specific Answers**:\n  - **(a) Generation Window**: UDIN must be generated at the time of signing, but in exceptional circumstances, it can be generated **within 60 days from the date of signing**.\n  - **(b) Revocation Protocol**: UDIN can be revoked by the member on the UDIN portal by selecting the document and entering the exact reason for revocation. Regulators/stakeholders verifying the revoked UDIN will see the status as *'Revoked'* along with the reason.\n  - **(c) Legal Consequence**: Issuing reports/certificates without generating UDIN or failing to generate it within the 60-day window is a direct contravention of Council guidelines, making the member **GUILTY of professional misconduct** under Clause (1) of Part II of the Second Schedule.",
